   "id": "numerical.lambda_a_decay",
   "kind": "numerical",
   "source": "research/rh/checkpoints/20261101_lambda_lab_s1/README.md",
   "statement": "Ritz upper bounds for the lowest eigenvalue of the Weil form on [-a, a]: lambda_a = 9.4e-7 (a = 0.5), 1.3e-12 (a = 11/16), <= 9.3e-42 (a = 2); on moment-zero packets 1.7e-7 at a = 11/16 and <= 1.4e-36 at a = 2; decay approaching exp(-4 pi e^{2a}).",
   "limits": "Upper bounds only; floating point at 200 digits, not interval-certified."
  },
  {
   "id": "numerical.simple_even_small_a",
   "kind": "numerical",
   "source": "research/rh/checkpoints/20261101_lambda_lab_s1/README.md",
   "statement": "For a = 0.3, 0.5, 0.6, 11/16 the lowest eigenvalue is simple (lambda2/lambda1 = 29 to 606) and its eigenvector is even.",
   "limits": "Finite basis N = 32."
  },
  {
   "id": "numerical.family_budget_must_decay",
   "kind": "numerical",
   "source": "research/rh/checkpoints/20261101_lambda_lab_s1/README.md",
   "statement": "Fine moment-zero packets span the moment-zero subspace of [-a, a]; with bounded overlap a family bound QW(sum g_i) >= c sum ||g_i||^2 with c independent of a would force lambda0_a >= c/2, which the computed upper bounds exclude.",
   "limits": "Argument written out in the README, not formalized; relies on the numerical upper bounds.",
   "depends_on": [
    "moment_killer.exists_momentKiller_packet",
    "numerical.lambda_a_decay"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "literature.yoshida_suzuki_continuity",
   "kind": "literature",
   "source": "Suzuki, arXiv 2606.09096, Thm 1.3 and the remark after it; Yoshida 1992",
   "statement": "lambda_a is continuous in a; RH holds iff the localized Weil form is nondegenerate for every a."
  },
  {
   "id": "literature.suzuki_small_a",
   "kind": "literature",
   "source": "Suzuki, arXiv 2606.09096, Thm 1.4",
   "statement": "For sufficiently small a the lowest eigenvalue is positive and simple, with an even eigenfunction."
  },
  {
   "id": "literature.ccm_spectral_triples",
   "kind": "literature",
   "source": "Connes, Consani, Moscovici, arXiv 2511.22755, Thm 1.1, Cor 3.8, Section 8",
   "statement": "If the lowest eigenvalue is simple with even eigenvector, the Fourier transform of that eigenvector has only real zeros; if lim mu_lambda = 0 then RH. Missing steps: simple-even for all lambda, and the prolate approximation of the eigenvector."
  },
